"comparison": "Both AVGO and AMD disclose that their IT systems and those of third parties are vulnerable to cyberattacks, including those leveraging AI, which could disrupt operations and expose sensitive data. AVGO specifically notes its dependence on vendors to address cybersecurity threats to their own systems, stating, 'we are, out of necessity, dependent on our vendors to adequately address cybersecurity threats to their own systems' (avgo_2024_1A_P031_S005). Similarly, AMD highlights its reliance on third-party IT systems and the vulnerability of confidential data processed by them: 'We own and manage some IT Systems but also rely on critical third-party IT Systems, products and services' and 'Our IT Systems and Confidential Data are vulnerable to a range of cybersecurity risks and threats... such as zero-day attacks' (amd_2024_1A_P055_S002, amd_2024_1A_P055_S009).",
